@startuml
title TMFC040: Product Usage Management -- eTOM/SID ABE Links

class "Product Usage Management" as ProductUsageManagement <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "Product Usage ABE" as ProductUsageABE <<SID Data Entity>>
class "Product Price ABE" as ProductPriceABE <<SID Data Entity>>

' eTOM activity <-> SID ABE links. Per the image's own legend, an arrow from the
' eTOM activity towards the SID ABE means information produced by the activity;
' the reverse arrow means information consumed by the activity.
' Product Usage ABE: the image draws a single double-headed arrow, i.e. both
' "produces" and "is consumed by" hold simultaneously.
ProductUsageManagement --> ProductUsageABE : produces
ProductUsageABE --> ProductUsageManagement : is consumed by

' Product Price ABE: the image draws a single, single-headed arrow pointing
' only towards the SID ABE -- "produces" only, with no return arrow drawn.
ProductUsageManagement --> ProductPriceABE : produces

@enduml
